---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Gallery"
  description="Explore Chudware modeling, CAM, and simulation examples, with requests, results, and full-size product screenshots."
>
  <header class="page-hero gallery-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Product gallery</p>
      <h1>Start with the request. Inspect the result.</h1>
      <p class="lede">See the request, the result, and the tools used to inspect it. Open any image at full size to read the feature tree, copilot, and study details.</p>
      <p class="gallery-disclosure">Modeling includes a recorded demo response. CAM and simulation use scripted examples; their requests describe those scenarios rather than quote a conversation. Every image is an unedited capture from the desktop app.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section gallery-section" aria-label="Chudware product examples">
    <div class="wrap gallery-stack">
      <article class="gallery-case" id="modeling" aria-labelledby="modeling-title">
        <header class="case-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">01 / Model</p>
            <h2 id="modeling-title">Build the tray. Leave every feature human-editable.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>A small tray with box, fillet, and shell features preserved as a dimension-driven, human-editable history.</p>
        </header>
        <div class="request-result">
          <section class="evidence-card request-card" aria-labelledby="modeling-request">
            <p class="evidence-label" id="modeling-request">Public demo request <span>(task excerpt)</span></p>
            <blockquote>&ldquo;Create a 60 &times; 40 &times; 10&nbsp;mm open-top tray. Fillet two vertical outside edges to 4&nbsp;mm, then shell it to a 2&nbsp;mm wall by removing the top face.&rdquo;</blockquote>
            <p class="evidence-note">Recorded in a new demo workspace. The screenshot includes the assistant's response.</p>
          </section>
          <section class="evidence-card result-card" aria-labelledby="modeling-result">
            <p class="evidence-label" id="modeling-result">Observed result</p>
            <p>The agents created one solid with editable box, fillet, and shell features; measured a 1.998&nbsp;mm minimum wall; passed its geometry verification; and saved the native <code>.step+</code> document. The deterministic capture reproduces the same feature sequence in the viewport.</p>
          </section>
        </div>
        <figure class="capture">
          <a class="capture-link" href="/images/modeling.png" aria-label="Open the full-size modeling capture">
            <img src="/images/modeling.png" width="1600" height="900" fetchpriority="high" alt="Chudware modeling workspace showing an open-top tray in the 3D viewport, an ordered Box1, Fillet1, and Shell1 feature tree on the left, and the full Copilot panel and composer on the right" />
          </a>
          <figcaption>
            <span>Modeling workspace · recorded demo response</span>
            <a class="text-link" href="/images/modeling.png">Open full size</a>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </article>

      <article class="gallery-case" id="cam" aria-labelledby="cam-title">
        <header class="case-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">02 / Manufacture</p>
            <h2 id="cam-title">Generate a milling job, then review the path.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>The CAM state stays explicit: stock, post, operations, tools, removal settings, and playhead are all visible before anything reaches a machine.</p>
        </header>
        <div class="request-result">
          <section class="evidence-card request-card" aria-labelledby="cam-request">
            <p class="evidence-label" id="cam-request">Example request</p>
            <blockquote>&ldquo;Prepare an 80 &times; 60 &times; 15&nbsp;mm plate with four &Oslash;5&nbsp;mm through-holes for a Fanuc mill. Generate the operations and pause the simulation halfway through.&rdquo;</blockquote>
            <p class="evidence-note">Suggested request for the scripted example below.</p>
          </section>
          <section class="evidence-card result-card" aria-labelledby="cam-result">
            <p class="evidence-label" id="cam-result">Observed result</p>
            <p>The job contains face, contour, and drill operations using a 10&nbsp;mm flat end mill and a 5&nbsp;mm drill. The viewport is paused at 50% (0:47 of 1:35), and the job remains visibly marked <strong>UNVERIFIED</strong>.</p>
          </section>
        </div>
        <figure class="capture">
          <a class="capture-link" href="/images/cam.png" aria-label="Open the full-size CAM capture">
            <img src="/images/cam.png" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" alt="Chudware Manufacture workspace showing a four-hole plate with toolpaths in the native viewport, face, contour, and drill operations in the Job Manager, a 50 percent simulation playhead, and the full Copilot panel and composer" />
          </a>
          <figcaption>
            <span>CAM workspace · scripted example</span>
            <a class="text-link" href="/images/cam.png">Open full size</a>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </article>

      <article class="gallery-case" id="simulation" aria-labelledby="simulation-title">
        <header class="case-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">03 / Simulate</p>
            <h2 id="simulation-title">Define the load case. Read the result with its mesh.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Inspect the stress contour alongside displacement, factor of safety, and mesh counts.</p>
        </header>
        <div class="request-result">
          <section class="evidence-card request-card" aria-labelledby="simulation-request">
            <p class="evidence-label" id="simulation-request">Example request</p>
            <blockquote>&ldquo;Run a static study on a 60 &times; 40 &times; 10&nbsp;mm steel block. Fix the &minus;X end face, apply 100&nbsp;N in &minus;Z to the +X end face, and show von Mises stress and displacement.&rdquo;</blockquote>
            <p class="evidence-note">Suggested request for the scripted example below.</p>
          </section>
          <section class="evidence-card result-card" aria-labelledby="simulation-result">
            <p class="evidence-label" id="simulation-result">Observed result</p>
            <p>The captured study reports its stress scale, peak displacement, minimum factor of safety, and node, element, and equation counts beside the contour. It is one scripted study result, not a benchmark or design sign-off.</p>
          </section>
        </div>
        <figure class="capture">
          <a class="capture-link" href="/images/fea.png" aria-label="Open the full-size simulation capture">
            <img src="/images/fea.png" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" alt="Chudware Simulate workspace showing a completed static study with a von Mises stress contour and scale, numeric stress, displacement, factor-of-safety, mesh and solver results, and the full Copilot panel and composer" />
          </a>
          <figcaption>
            <span>Static stress study · scripted example</span>
            <span><a class="text-link" href="/images/fea.png">Open full size</a> &middot; <a class="text-link" href="/product/simulation/">Simulation details</a></span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .gallery-hero h1 { max-width: 12ch; }
  .gallery-disclosure { max-width: 76ch; margin-top: var(--s5); padding-left: var(--s4); border-left: var(--border-strong) solid var(--technical); color: var(--faint); font: var(--step--1)/1.6 var(--mono); }
  .gallery-stack { display: grid; gap: clamp(var(--s9), 12vw, calc(var(--s10) * 1.5)); }
  .gallery-case { min-width: 0; scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--header-height) + var(--s5)); }
  .case-heading { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .95fr) minmax(18rem, .55fr); gap: clamp(var(--s5), 6vw, var(--s9)); align-items: end; padding-top: var(--s5); border-top: var(--border-strong) solid var(--line-hi); }
  .case-heading > div { display: grid; gap: var(--s3); }
  .case-heading h2 { max-width: 18ch; }
  .case-heading > p { max-width: 48ch; color: var(--muted); }
  .request-result { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin-top: var(--s6); border: var(--border) solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--surface); overflow: hidden; }
  .evidence-card { display: grid; align-content: start; gap: var(--s3); min-width: 0; padding: clamp(var(--s4), 3vw, var(--s6)); }
  .evidence-card + .evidence-card { border-left: var(--border) solid var(--line); }
  .request-card { box-shadow: inset var(--border-strong) 0 var(--accent); }
  .result-card { box-shadow: inset var(--border-strong) 0 var(--technical); }
  .evidence-label { color: var(--faint); font: 400 var(--step--2)/1.4 var(--mono); letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  blockquote { color: var(--text); font-size: var(--step-1); line-height: 1.55; text-wrap: pretty; }
  .result-card > p:last-child { color: var(--muted); }
  .result-card strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 650; }
  .evidence-note { color: var(--faint); font: var(--step--2)/1.55 var(--mono); }
  .capture { margin-top: var(--s5); padding: var(--s2); border: var(--border) solid var(--line-hi); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--surface); box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .capture-link { display: block; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); background: var(--bg-deep); overflow: hidden; }
  .capture img { width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); }
  .capture figcaption { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: var(--s2) var(--s5); padding: var(--s3) var(--s2) var(--s1); color: var(--faint); font: var(--step--1)/1.5 var(--mono); }
  .capture figcaption .text-link { font-family: var(--sans); }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .case-heading, .request-result { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .case-heading { align-items: start; gap: var(--s4); }
    .case-heading > p { max-width: var(--measure); }
    .evidence-card + .evidence-card { border-top: var(--border) solid var(--line); border-left: 0; }
    .capture { margin-inline: calc(var(--gutter) * -.5); padding: var(--s1); }
    .capture figcaption { align-items: flex-start; flex-direction: column; padding-inline: var(--s3); }
  }
</style>
